     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yes. The easiest way to do that these days is by creating an <a href=\"http://htmlwidgets.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://htmlwidgets.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399827114000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3LCzTqo4c_U5Lx0LjHC4t-\">htmlwidget</a>. Here&#39;s a simple example that uses d3:<div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://jcheng.shinyapps.io/cranbubbles/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jcheng.shinyapps.io/cranbubbles/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399827114000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0mZpnzKJCNuVYQuAMVkbOZ\">https://jcheng.shinyapps.io/cranbubbles/</a><br></div><div>Source: <a href=\"https://github.com/jcheng5/bubbles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/jcheng5/bubbles&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792399827114000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3BCNs_DkcP9O-hqYnv17fs\">https://github.com/jcheng5/bubbles</a><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
